    "question": "Earlier questions: Explain what outline.rs:1\u201346 does and how it works. \u2192 How does Font::memory_face choose a format and create a usable face? Start with its ordered dispatch and invalid input or face-index branches. Then explain which SFNT tables are required, how missing tables differ from malformed table contents, and where errors propagate. Show the real code paths and useful diagrams.. Current question: In src/font.rs, show how the PFR0 prefix branch in Font::memory_face sends the incoming bytes to pfr_face. Make this a short narrated HTML visual story with an input/header representation and its consequence. Explain only this dispatch branch; do not investigate PFR internals or unrelated formats. Use a graph only if it teaches something that the header representation cannot.",
